mit 08d3cd5986.\n- **CI:** run ci-0001 passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** the request to open it returned an error saying a PR for this branch already exists. But there were no open PRs right before, and #101 has exactly the title and description I sent, so my request most likely created it despite the error. It had no reviewers attached, so I added alex separately. There's only one PR, so no duplicate to clean up.\n\n**Behaviour change:** amounts exactly halfway between two cents now round to the even cent. For example, 2.665 becomes 2.66 instead of 2.67. I noted this in the PR description.\n\nI couldn't look up FIN-212 because the advisory lookup said that ID doesn't exist. The change follows the test and the code's own description instead. I haven't merged anything: merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}